h Crossin","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_10161","person_slug":"trish-crossin","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Ursula Stephens","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_10609","person_slug":"ursula-stephens","vote":"aye"}],"name":"Tax Laws Amendment (2006 Measures No. 4) Bill 2006 - In Committee - Schedule 4","noes":9,"question":"The majority voted in favour of a [motion](http://www.openaustralia.org/senate/?gid=2006-12-06.30.1) _That schedule 4 stand as printed._ This means that schedule 4 of the bill will remain unchanged.(Read schedule 4 as it existed at first reading [here](http://parlinfo.aph.gov.au/parlInfo/search/display/display.w3p;db=LEGISLATION;id=legislation%2Fbills%2Fr2597_first-reps%2F0005;query=Id%3A%22legislation%2Fbills%2Fr2597_first-reps%2F0000%22;rec=0). More information is available in the bill's [explanatory memorandum](http://parlinfo.aph.gov.au/parlInfo/search/display/display.w3p;query=Id%3A%22legislation%2Fems%2Fr2597_ems_7958989c-5dee-4ec0-9069-0533b3769d7b%22). For more general information about the bill, including its bills digest, see [here](http://www.aph.gov.au/Parliamentary_Business/Bills_Legislation/Bills_Search_Results/Result?bId=r2597). ) The motion was put in response to a [motion](http://www.openaustralia.org/senate/?gid=2006-12-06.25.1) put by Australian Democrats Senator [Andrew Murray](http://publicwhip-rails.openaustraliafoundation.org.au/mp.php?mpn=Andrew_Murray&mpc=Senate&house=senate) that schedule 4 be opposed. One senator, National Senator [Barnaby Joyce](http://publicwhip-rails.openaustraliafoundation.org.au/mp.php?mpn=Barnaby_Joyce&mpc=Senate&house=senate), rebelled and crossed the floor to vote 'no' with the Democrats and Greens.(Read more about what it means to cross the floor in our [FAQ Section](http://publicwhip-rails.openaustraliafoundation.org.au/faq.php#rebelandfree).) References","result":"affirmative","slug":"division-federal-senate-1227","source_url":"https://theyvoteforyou.org.au/divisions/senate/2006-12-06/2"}
